|~ `::absent`, the mark in a shape of a key some records lack, and the
   laws declared under it.
   The rules it holds: [QSDSP#residence]. ~|

:absent
  |~~ An absent marks, in the shape of a value, a key that some of the
      records merged there hold and others lack, over the shape of what
      the records that hold it hold:
      `[{:a 1} {:a 2 :b "x"}] | shape` answers
      `::shape[{:a ::number :b ::absent::string}]`. Records that share a
      key merge so, the keys of all of them in one record and a key some
      lack marked, whatever their order; records that share no key stand
      apart as the kinds where the elements part. The mark stands as well
      over the element of a vector or a set that is empty in some of the
      data, its first index missing there,
      `[{:labels [{:name "bug"}]} {:labels []}] | shape` answering
      `::shape[{:labels [::absent{:name ::string}]}]`. A part the mark
      stands over may be missing from the data, so `get` refuses it where
      it is and `query` reads it softly; the mark stands outside
      `::nullable`.
      ::link~(::shape | doc) ::link~(::nullable | doc)
      ::link~(::any/query | doc)
  ~~|
  ::kind
    | proves :marksAKeySomeRecordsLack
        |~~ A key some records lack stands marked absent. ~~|
        ~([{:a 1} {:a 2 :b "x"}] | shape | eq ::shape[{:a ::number :b ::absent::string}])
    | proves :marksTheElementOfAVectorEmptyInSome
        |~~ The element of a vector empty in some of the data is absent. ~~|
        ~([{:labels [{:name "bug"}]} {:labels []}] | shape | eq ::shape[{:labels [::absent{:name ::string}]}])
    | proves :standsOutsideTheNullMark
        |~~ A key missing from some records and null in others is absent
            outside and nullable within.
        ~~|
        ~([{:a 1} {:a null} {}] | shape | eq ::shape[{:a ::absent::nullable::number}])
